  "details": "Issue: Remote avatars in desktop mode have an IK jitter that looks like a 'sprinkler' motion. \n\nBranches: On the Open Beta and Internal (1645) branches and previously in 1644. I have not confirmed if this happens on Live.\n\nOther notes: \n\n-I am unsure if this can happen when viewing your own avatar on desktop mode, whether it's viewed at via Mirror, Camera, avatar preview, or other third-person tool.\n\n-The jitter will stop if the user turns or moves their avatar\n\nIn my drive folder, I have named these videos \"164XAvatarSprinkler\" and \"1645AvatarSprinkler\".",
